<h2>1. Information on this website</h2>
<p>
  We try to keep the information on this website correct and up to date, but we
  do not guarantee that it is complete or free of errors. Programme plans and
  targets describe goals, not results already achieved.
</p>

<h2>2. Tax benefits</h2>
<p>
  <%= trust.name %> will issue tax-exemption receipts under Section 80G of the
  Income Tax Act only after it receives 80G approval. Until then, donations do
  not carry any promised tax benefit. Please check with your tax adviser.
</p>

<h2>3. Medical help</h2>
<p>
  The Trust is not a hospital or medical provider and does not give medical
  advice. Financial help for treatment depends on verification and available
  funds, and is not guaranteed.
</p>

<h2>4. External links and services</h2>
<p>
  Payments are processed by PayU and emails are sent through a third-party
  provider. The Trust is not responsible for their content, availability or
  privacy practices.
</p>

<h2>5. Independence</h2>
<p>
  <%= trust.name %> is an independent charitable trust. It is not linked to
  any company, political party or government body.
</p>

